# Ask the coordinator whether it will handle a finished utterance.
#
# The voice node calls this once per recognised user utterance that is not
# a motion, stop or sleep command, before it generates a conversational
# reply.  The call is bounded (a few seconds) and fails open: if the
# coordinator is missing or slow the voice node answers normally, so a
# coordinator failure never silences Buddy or touches the stop path.
#
# claimed=true means the coordinator handled it (a vision question, an
# object-teaching step, a refused approach...) and reply is what Buddy
# should say. claimed=false means "answer it as ordinary conversation".

string request_id
string text
float32 confidence
string speaker_id
---
bool claimed
string reply
string intent
uint8 error_code
